  "answer": "As a financial education advisor using synthetic USD data, I can explain your debt projection task and state the limitations. We cannot invent sources, probabilities, affordability, or successful actions, and no payment execution is available. The supported projection model uses a fixed APR and payments, rounds monthly interest to cents before a month-end payment, includes no fees or new borrowing, and uses a default 1200-month horizon where time-varying payments are unsupported. Money is measured in integer cents, APR is a percentage, and values are validated. Regarding your question about skipping an extra payment next month and providing an exact new payoff date, our model does not support time-varying payments and cannot project a future change to your payment amount. Therefore, I cannot calculate an exact new payoff date for skipped or altered future payments.",
  "facts": []
}

